The names of the current user interface header files, their locations,
and which functions are declared in each of them is likely to change.
This is an attempt to document the current state.

@section uiio.h

This file declares the public interface to the user interface abstraction.

@defun uiio_init (UIIO *uiio) @arrow{} bool
Responsible for early initialization of the current user interface routines.
@b{MUST} be called before @b{any} other @code{uiio_} routines.
@end defun

@defun uiio_pre_database_init (UIIO *uiio, bool runningInterpreter) @arrow{} bool
@end defun

@defun uiio_post_database_init (UIIO *uiio) @arrow{} void
Responsible for any user interface initialization that is to be done @b{after}
a database is successfully opened.
@end defun

@defun uiio_shutdown_ui (UIIO *uiio, bool pause) @arrow{} void
Called when a user interface is being shutdown.  Examples would be
when the user interface is changing to a different interface or the
program is about to exit.
@end defun

@defvar current_uiio @arrow{} UIIO*
This points to the current user interface input/output structure.
Currently, there are two @code{UIIO*}'s that are defined --
@code{uiio_curses} and @code{uiio_stdio}.  There might be additional
@code{UIIO*}'s in the future -- such as for a @code{GUI} (graphical
user interface) or for a @code{CLI} (command line interface).
@end defvar

@defvar uiio_curses @arrow{} UIIO*
The curses user interface input/output structure.  Used by
@command{llines}.
@end defvar

@defvar uiio_stdio @arrow{} UIIO*
The stdio user interface input/output structure.  Used by @command{llexec}.
@end defvar

